# Browser game test hygiene

- Run interactive game tests only in the Codex in-app browser, as required by `AGENTS.md`.
- Keep every agent-controlled Codex in-app browser tab silent at all times.
- Disable the page or game's master sound before gameplay or any interaction that can unlock audio. Prefer a supported `sound=0` test-route parameter; otherwise turn sound off in the page settings first.
- Never enable sound or use `sound=1` in an agent-controlled browser, even for an audible check. If a page cannot be kept silent, stop browser work and report the limitation.
- After the required checks and evidence are complete, close every in-app browser tab opened by the agent for that test.
- Never close a tab opened by the user or another task, and do not keep a finished test tab alive as a deliverable or handoff.
- Stop a local preview or development server that was started only for the finished browser test.
